==English==

===Etymology===
{{named-after|en|Satoshi Nakamoto|wplink==}}, the pseudonymous designer of [[bitcoin|Bitcoin]], from {{bor|en|ja|さとし|tr=Satoshi}}, nominalization of the classical adjective {{m|ja|聡し|tr=satoshi}}, modern {{m|ja|聡い|tr=satoi||[[clever]], [[smart]], [[sharp]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{homophones|en|Satoshi}}
* {{IPA|en|/saˈtowʃi/|/sɐˈtowʃɪ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|*}}

# A hundred-millionth (10{{sup|−8}}) of a {{l|en|bitcoin}}; the same as 10 nanocoins (nBTC) or 10{{sup|−8}} BTC.
#: {{syn|en|sat}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|millisatoshi}}

